      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T03:31:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One `None` here aborts the whole move. `HardwareDispatcher.get_bios_attribute` (`dispatchers/hardware.py:95`) swallows Badfish exceptions and returns None, and `get_request` (`tools/external/badfish.py:115`) does not retry, so a single transient 503 or connection error during a power cycle fails the rebuild at hardware_prep. `_wait_for_bootmode` below already treats None as keep-polling; giving the initial read the same 2 to 3 attempts would make it as forgiving as the loop.",
      "revId": "da4e82ee1848b9f14fc22399d80d76d670e3bc8c",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
